{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator poll method blender operator poll method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Poll Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Poll Method","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Add-On Architecture]] · [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Architecture","Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender bContext Structure","Blender Operator Exec Callback","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator poll method blender operator poll method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Poll Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Poll Method","heading":"Blender Operator Poll Method","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A `poll` class method determines whether an operator or panel is available in the current Blender context. It can test conditions such as Edit Mode, object type, or the presence of a suitable active object and return a Boolean that controls visibility or executability.\n\nPolling makes invalid actions unavailable before execution rather than requiring every failure to be handled after a button is pressed. Because Blender reevaluates interface drawing as context changes, a panel guarded by `poll` can appear precisely when its tools are meaningful.\n\nThe core implementation stores the poll function on the [[Blender Operator Type Structure]]. Event handling calls it with the active [[Blender bContext Structure]] before the [[Blender Operator Exec Callback]], so editor location, current mode, and active data can prevent an otherwise registered operation from running.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Architecture","Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender bContext Structure","Blender Operator Exec Callback","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender operator poll method blender operator poll method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Operator Poll Method.md","fileName":"Blender Operator Poll Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Operator Poll Method","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]\n\n[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Add-On Architecture","Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Type Structure","Blender bContext Structure","Blender Operator Exec Callback","blenderpythonapi.pdf","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}